        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Literary Translation: Fidelity and Freedom",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE INVISIBLE TRANSLATOR PROBLEM:\n  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ Anglo-American literary culture prizes the \"fluent\"        │\n  │ translation — reading as if originally in English.         │\n  │ The translator's labor disappears into the text.           │\n  │ Venuti: this is cultural imperialism at sentence level.    │\n  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
